  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On a vast grassland, red colored fire beard grass grows everywhere.",
      "chapters": [
        2103
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the ant plague, the largest fire beard grassland has perished into ruins, with no fire beard grass left even at the roots, and vermilion flame wolves and red grass horses are nearly extinct.",
      "chapters": [
        2106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Resources left in the grotto-heaven include twenty-eight charcoal lakes distributed across it, a huge fire date forest, and ancient desolate plant giant disaster blazing trees covered in raging flames.",
      "chapters": [
        2108
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On a vast grassland, red fire beard grass is in harvest when Gu Masters of the grotto-heaven start collecting it. Ants rise from underground, some finger-sized and some as large as carriages, and engulf the grassland. Among the two heavens’ grotto-heavens hit by the plague, this one’s owner is listed as a main target with Old Immortal Hua Yu and Granny Skeleton.",
      "chapters": [
        2103
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "char_old_immortal_hua_yu",
        "char_granny_skeleton"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fire Plain Grotto Lord flies back through immemorial white heaven after suppressing the ant plague in his body. The largest fire beard grassland has already perished. Vermilion flame wolves and red grass horses are nearly extinct. He belongs to the Righteous Qi Alliance and must spend contribution points to salvage the grotto-heaven. He concludes that all grotto-heavens in the two heavens are now Fang Yuan’s prey.",
      "chapters": [
        2106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grotto-lords-return",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fire_plain_grotto_lord",
        "fac_righteous_qi_alliance",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan opens a huge entrance through brute force. The heavenly spirit is a rabbit, dazed from a nine heavens fragment, then frantic with fear. Gu Immortals inside find the Grotto Lord’s life tablet Gu and soul lantern Gu destroyed. Fang Yuan cannot enter himself because of dao mark conflict, so subordinates led by Fairy Miao Yin and Lady White Rabbit charge in.",
      "chapters": [
        2107
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "forced-entrance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "gu_soul_lantern_gu",
        "char_fairy_miao_yin",
        "char_lady_white_rabbit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It cultivates fire path primarily. Resources include twenty-eight charcoal lakes, a fire date forest, and luck path materials such as giant disaster blazing trees. It is a human grotto-heaven with over a hundred million purebred humans. After the remaining Gu Immortals are killed, Fang Yuan orders those people killed to construct Human Sea, then annexes the grotto-heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        2108
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "human-population",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_human_sea"
      ]
    }
  ],
